<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The Distronode mark, generated from the square logo lockup the website serves into the
  five density buckets.

  ⛔ THE FOREGROUND IS A 108dp CANVAS WITH THE MARK AT 52dp IN THE MIDDLE, AND THE PADDING
  IS LOAD-BEARING RATHER THAN TASTE. Adaptive icons reserve the outer 18dp on every edge
  for the launcher's mask and its parallax, so artwork placed there is clipped on some
  launchers and not others. The mark is held slightly inside even the 72dp safe zone
  at Material's square keyline, because its blades run out to the edges of their own
  bounding box: at 62dp it is visibly pressed against the circular mask.

  ⚠️ PNG rather than a vector: the mark is a gradient-filled spiral with no flat-fill
  equivalent, so tracing it to `pathData` would either lose the gradient or grow into
  something nobody can hand-edit. `minSdk` is 26 and adaptive icons landed in 26, so no
  density-bucketed raster fallback for pre-26 is needed.

  ⚠️ `monochrome` intentionally reuses the same drawable. Android 13+ themed icons take
  only the alpha channel, so the silhouette is what ships; it reads as the spiral.
-->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@color/ic_launcher_background" />
    <foreground android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground" />
    <monochrome android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground" />
</adaptive-icon>
